{"t": 220.67, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 1, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "SECE", "rationale": "Synchronous Electric Charge Extraction (SECE) is highly efficient for piezo harvesting. It extracts the available charge from the transducer capacitance at each voltage peak using an inductor and a switch, transferring it to the output capacitor via a diode. This avoids the continuous diode drops of a full-bridge rectifier and allows the output voltage to be decoupled from the piezo's open-circuit voltage, which is essential for meeting both the 1.8V minimum and 3.6V maximum across all load conditions.", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "SECE", "rationale": "Synchronous Electric Charge Extraction (SECE) is highly efficient for piezo harvesting. It extracts the available charge from the transducer capacitance at each voltage peak using an inductor and a switch, transferring it to the output capacitor via a diode. This avoids the continuous diode drops of a full-bridge rectifier and allows the output voltage to be decoupled from the piezo's open-circuit voltage, which is essential for meeting both the 1.8V minimum and 3.6V maximum across all load conditions.", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "S2", "type": "S", "nodes": ["pzn", "n1"], "ctrl": "G2"}, {"id": "L1", "type": "L", "nodes": ["n1", "n2"], "value": 0.0022}, {"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["n2", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "C1", "type": "C", "nodes": ["out", "0"], "value": 4.7e-06}, {"id": "DZ1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "out"], "model": "DZ33"}, {"id": "G1", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 3e-05, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "pos"}, {"id": "G2", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 3e-05, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "neg"}]}}
